 "flightLifeNote": "2026-09-29 FP: stroke pitch capped. Hips lat 14 swung the Hips->Head axis 13.5-39.4 deg over the stroke, which on the battle camera read as a dive/tumble. Hips 5, Neck -5 in the same phase (the neck holds its world angle), Head 3: the head stays near level and the heave carries the bob. Hind legs: quadrupedSit.tuck.hind 80 -> 60, UpLeg swing 24 -> 12, Leg -16 -> -8 (main review 2026-09-29): at 80 + 24 the lion legs folded above the back line (rump-up / dead-bug); now they trail back about level, a leaping lion stretched out. v5 (main review 2026-09-29): Move flies level - the rest mesh's eagle forepart stands upright, so Spine1 +22 / Neck +10 bend it forward and Head -22 keeps the beak level (mesh body axis hind->chest +22..+32 -> +10..+21, DEF plates +3..+22); Leg +35 trails the hind legs back instead of hanging. AttackFront is an authored rear-and-strike in DEF timing (flightLife keys): Spine -14 at x 0.29 (rear, wings spread high: wingChain open/flap keys, WingL/R_00 lift keys) then +46 at 0.57 (lunge, head leading low via Neck/Head keys, wings closing back), recovered by 0.86; the wings' raised-lift no longer brackets AttackFront. Idle / Hitted as v4 (raised wings, flinch). Mesh body axis per 1/8 clip: 75 74 64 36 9 49 69 75 (DEF sit / rear / drive / lunge / recover). 2026-09-29 standing (s5): the sit clips now hold the DEF's rampant stand - quadrupedSit pitched upright on the planted hind legs, forelegs (Arm +30 / ForeArm -60) raised with talons forward, Neck -5 / Head -25 so the head sits up rather than curling forward, wings folded and raised behind the back (Idle/Mouseover fold/droop offsets, matched at the first/last key of every clip that enters or leaves the sit). Reviewed against the DEF standing frame from the battle camera (V:/olden_fp_work/stands5/<unit>_standing_sheet.png); residual: the Meshy wings are longer than the DEF's, so the raised fold reads taller.",
 "groundNote": "2026-09-29 FP (main review): the DEF idle (02_00) rears on its hind legs ON the ground, and flight belongs to Move / MoveStart / MoveEnd only. The quadruped fit's free vertical screen offset had lifted every ground clip +13..+18 px (Idle mesh floor 0.135 above z=0, about 13% of the height). quadruped.fit.groundClips pins that dy to 0. Tail: flightLife QTail_00 lat offset +25 in the ground clips lifts the tail root, because the sit's 'keep' tail drops with the rear and its curl went 0.09-0.11 of the height below z=0 (sink_probe 2026-09-29). dyEase MoveEnd out / Death in: the landing ends on the idle floor and Death enters from the stance (the free fit had griffin MoveEnd rise 7 -> 15 px and end 0.22 of the height up, then pop down into Idle). 2026-09-29 (fleet ground_glb): the tail lift is held in EVERY clip, not only the ground clips: with Idle grounded, MoveEnd's and Death's entry tail (QTail_02) hung 0.13-0.18 of the height below the body as the lowest vertex, so ground apply lifted those clips and their Hips stepped past the DEF allowance (battle MoveEnd +0.203 vs 0.125, Death +0.132 vs 0.040; base Death +0.109). Held everywhere, no clip boundary pops. Death also enters unrolled (dyEase 'in' eases the side roll: a free 30 deg roll at key 0 put the Hips +0.07 above Idle's).",
